/tmp/tmp.bEoUxnvCNB/src/pattern_domination.tex:166:Note that many well-studied domination variants represent a special case of Pattern $k$-Dominating Set for a fixed graph $H$ (e.g. $k$-Induced Matching Dominating Set, $k$-Clique Dominating Set, $k$-Independent Dominating Set, etc.), and due to the previous corollary, we can solve any such \emph{$H$-Pattern $k$-Dominating Set} problem in the claimed time, as long as $H$ admits a perfect matching. 
/tmp/tmp.bEoUxnvCNB/src/pattern_domination.tex:167:Most notably, this gives us a tool to efficiently solve \emph{Clique $k$-Dominating Set} for any even $k$ in sparse graphs \footnote{For odd $k\geq 5$, we remark that only additional overhead of $\frac{m}{n}$ suffices, by observing that there is a heavy vertex in any such dominating set and that the remaining vertices form a $(k-1)$-clique.}.
