/tmp/tmp.bEoUxnvCNB/src/introduction.tex:163:So far we mentioned the full classification of three structurally very different choices of patterns $H$, that all fall into one of the two extreme regimes of being either as hard as the general $k$-Pattern Domination problem, or being as easy as any pattern can be. %\mirza{Maybe we should rephrase this sentence a bit, but I kinda like the idea of going in this direction.}
/tmp/tmp.bEoUxnvCNB/src/introduction.tex:167:As our last contribution, we answer this question negatively (assuming $k$-OV hypothesis), by tightly classifying the $k$-Induced Matching Domination problem that lies in neither of those two regimes, unless $k$-OV hypothesis fails.
