%    When the input graph is sparse, however, we can obtain a significant polynomial improvement and a running time of $m^{r}n^{k-2r+o(1)}$ and prove that this running time cannot be improved unless $3$-Uniform Hyperclique Hypothesis fails. 
%    For the latter regime, we demonstrate a randomized algorithm solving this problem in "$k$-clique" running time ($n^{\omega k/3+o(1)}$), and we show that any significant improvement over this running time would refute the $k$-Clique hypothesis.
