\section{Preliminaries}
\label{sec:prelims}
Let $n$ be a positive integer. 
We denote by $[n]$ the set $\{1,\dots, n\}$. 
If $S$ is an $n$-element set and $0\leq k\leq n$ is an integer, then $\binom{S}{k}$ denotes the set of all $k$-element subsets of $S$.

%We use $\Tilde{\bigO}$ notation, which hides the poly-logarithmic factors. 
