    "Section 3.2 defines r-Multiple k-Orthogonal Vectors and states that r=1 is "
    "exactly k-OV.  Its hardness lemma covers r<=k-2 and arbitrary unbalanced "
    "set sizes; the preceding algorithm section gives an efficient matrix-product "
    "route after reduction to domination, so the generated structured distribution "
    "is not claimed as Track A.  The same section's reduction proves that selected "
    "vectors with a zero in every coordinate correspond to an r-multiple dominating "
    "set.  Here the answer is sampled first, cyclic XOR identities are composed, and "
    "each identity is represented by four clauses.  Complete assignment blocks make "
    "planted and decoy rows exactly symmetric.  Balanced parity quartets defeat "
    "literal-frequency and row-weight outliers; random block and row orders defeat "
    "visible-order guesses; greedy coverage and random restarts are measured; the "
    "reference Gauss-Jordan solver succeeds as Track B requires."
)


# Updated after the three script-owned hardening runs.  These are diagnostics,
# not assertions used by verify().
G9_ORACLE_RESULTS = {
    "bare": {"solved": 0, "attempts": 0},
    "hinted": {"solved": 0, "attempts": 0},
    "placebo": {"solved": 0, "attempts": 0},
    "hinted_verdict": "not_run",
