codex
Implemented a self-contained Track B generator based on the paper’s \(r=1\) Multiple \(k\)-Orthogonal Vectors problem from Section 3.2.

Files:

- [gen_2409_08037.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.08037/gen_2409_08037.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.08037/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.08037/README.md)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.08037/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.08037/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.08037/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local results:

- All deterministic gates pass.
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000; exact density \(2^{-95}\).
- Four attacks: 0/8 each.
- Reference algorithm: 8/8, maximum 93,727 Boolean operations.
- Compact cyclic-invariant route: 288 operations.
- Answer: 56 characters, 24 elements.
- G8: 80/80 relabellings preserved; 20/20 unrelated keys distinct.

The result is not yet shippable: every bare, hinted, and placebo OpenRouter call returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded.” Consequently, there are zero counted oracle attempts and no valid hardening verdict. The script-owned error transcripts are preserved and the README explicitly records this blocker. Once the OpenRouter quota is restored, the three hardening runs must be repeated. The mathematical basis was checked against the [full paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2409.08037v1).
