codex
Implemented and locally verified a Track B generator based on the paper’s native \(r\)-Multiple \(k\)-Orthogonal Vectors problem from Definition 16 and Lemma 17. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2409.08037v1)

Deliverables:

- [gen_2409_08037.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.08037/gen_2409_08037.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.08037/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.08037/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.08037/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.08037/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.08037/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local results:

- All G1–G9 deterministic gates pass.
- Hard answer space: \(2^{59}\); random guesses: 0/200,000.
- Four failing attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Gaussian reference: 8/8, at most 33,001 counted operations.
- Plain DPLL: 8/8, up to 445 nodes and 808,167 literal inspections.
- Compact cyclic route: 298 operations.
- Canonical-key checks: 120/120 invariant transformations; 20/20 unrelated keys distinct.

External blocker: all bare, hinted, and placebo oracle redraws returned HTTP 403 due exhausted OpenRouter key limits, producing zero counted attempts. Therefore the module is locally complete but not yet shippable, and no `REJECTED.md` was created. The temporary G9 directories were moved to trash after their transcripts were copied.
