codex
Implemented and verified the Track B generator based on the paper’s \(r=1\) Multiple \(k\)-Orthogonal Vectors problem ([Definition 3.10, Section 3.2](https://arxiv.org/html/2409.08037)).

Deliverables:

- [gen_2409_08037.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.08037/gen_2409_08037.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.08037/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.08037/README.md)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.08037/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.08037/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2409.08037/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Results:

- All deterministic G1–G9(c) gates pass.
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000; exact witness density \(2^{-59}\).
- Four attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Reference Gaussian solver: 8/8, at most 33,001 counted operations.
- Plain DPLL: 8/8, up to 445 nodes and 808,167 literal operations.
- Intended structural route: 298 operations.
- Answer: 37 characters worst case, 12 elements.
- Independent exhaustive/reference testing passed 112 small cases.
- Canonical keys were distinct across an additional 200-instance audit.

The result is not yet shippable because OpenRouter rejected every bare, hinted, and placebo call with HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded.” Consequently, all three transcripts contain authentic script-generated error records but zero counted oracle attempts, and no hardness verdict. The README records this blocker and leaves `SHIPPING_DIFFICULTY="hard"` provisional.
